1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,720
Yo, what's up?

2
00:00:06,780 --> 00:00:08,000
Good afternoon, big brother.

3
00:00:09,360 --> 00:00:11,740
Yukimura, what are you doing in that butler get-up?

4
00:00:12,020 --> 00:00:15,280
It's part of the training that's listed in Becoming a Real Man, Volume 2.

5
00:00:15,580 --> 00:00:18,820
Though my skills have not quite matured, I am devoted, sir.

6
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:20,720
Look, this has nothing to do with maturity.

7
00:00:20,880 --> 00:00:22,380
You're a girl, you can't do this.

8
00:00:22,580 --> 00:00:24,680
My body's simply a home for my heart, sir.

9
00:00:24,780 --> 00:00:26,600
A true man can transcend biology.

10
00:00:26,760 --> 00:00:28,240
Don't let anyone tell you differently.

11
00:00:28,240 --> 00:00:32,160
Science determined that you're female, but the truth of your soul knows who you are.

12
00:00:32,260 --> 00:00:35,540
If in your heart you long to be the man you admire, don't let that dream go.

13
00:00:35,560 --> 00:00:35,980
Thank you.

14
00:00:36,640 --> 00:00:38,280
I'm going to make you proud of me.

15
00:00:38,500 --> 00:00:39,360
I'll never give up.

16
00:00:39,700 --> 00:00:40,700
You're my inspiration.

17
00:00:41,380 --> 00:00:43,300
I hope to be a man just like you someday.

18
00:02:14,843 --> 00:02:22,963
Okay, I can appreciate your dedication, but the clothes don't make sense.

19
00:02:23,403 --> 00:02:24,443
What's with the butler thing?

20
00:02:24,483 --> 00:02:26,443
A butler represents the most capable man.

21
00:02:26,723 --> 00:02:27,603
Capable of what?

22
00:02:27,623 --> 00:02:28,663
Who cares? It's fine.

23
00:02:28,863 --> 00:02:31,283
Girls in butler costumes are totes adorable, and you know it.

24
00:02:31,303 --> 00:02:32,543
Especially pretty girls.

25
00:02:32,723 --> 00:02:35,123
It's actually become kind of a popular trend lately.

26
00:02:35,283 --> 00:02:36,083
Like Black Butler.

27
00:02:36,323 --> 00:02:39,923
Everyone loves that, so you're instantly cool if you dress like those characters, even the girls.

28
00:02:39,963 --> 00:02:42,003
Or like that Chicken Butler in Mayonnaise Show.

29
00:02:42,003 --> 00:02:44,323
All girls want to be Coco no Emebaru.

30
00:02:44,843 --> 00:02:49,383
I love how even though she tries to act all sophist, she can't hide how awkward she is.

31
00:02:49,683 --> 00:02:51,903
And if she's pissed, everyone knows about it.

32
00:02:52,003 --> 00:02:53,963
Everything she does is so sexy!

33
00:02:54,303 --> 00:02:58,923
The way she manages to get covered in mayonnaise every five seconds and has to change her shirt makes me think,

34
00:02:59,123 --> 00:03:00,583
oh, you want it bad, you know?

35
00:03:01,283 --> 00:03:03,403
And we can know she would say yes to that.

36
00:03:03,443 --> 00:03:05,303
I wish I was as cute as Maybaru.

37
00:03:05,463 --> 00:03:06,883
I mean, is there anyone hotter?

38
00:03:08,243 --> 00:03:10,423
So yeah, that was a good call you made, Yozara.

39
00:03:11,003 --> 00:03:14,763
Yukimura in a butler suit is going to do wonders for her social life.

40
00:03:14,843 --> 00:03:19,083
Great. Guess I screwed that up, too.

41
00:03:19,383 --> 00:03:21,383
I'm sorry. That all went over my head.

42
00:03:21,503 --> 00:03:23,403
But I'm pleased to wear the clothes I was given.

43
00:03:23,603 --> 00:03:26,343
I only hope they allow me to serve you as best I can.

44
00:03:26,763 --> 00:03:27,403
Right on.

45
00:03:27,803 --> 00:03:29,243
Well, you have my support.

46
00:03:30,903 --> 00:03:31,223
Huh?

47
00:03:31,223 --> 00:03:32,663
What are you doing?

48
00:03:33,043 --> 00:03:35,143
Looks like one of those boys love games.

49
00:03:35,383 --> 00:03:36,143
Yes, it is.

50
00:03:36,263 --> 00:03:39,363
Rika thought she'd try to sort through some of her game backlog while she can.

51
00:03:39,563 --> 00:03:41,323
Are they all dude-on-dude games?

52
00:03:41,603 --> 00:03:42,503
No, not at all.

53
00:03:42,683 --> 00:03:46,063
There are some RPGs, some shooters, and some otomege, too.

54
00:03:46,723 --> 00:03:47,963
Wait, what was that last one?

55
00:03:48,023 --> 00:03:49,123
Otomege? What's that?

56
00:03:49,123 --> 00:03:52,703
Where the main character is a girl and she tries to date as many boys as she can.

57
00:03:53,483 --> 00:03:54,643
Uh, no.

58
00:03:54,903 --> 00:03:56,283
It's, it's that game.

59
00:03:56,543 --> 00:03:58,223
The Simoponome crap from before.

60
00:03:58,823 --> 00:03:59,943
That looks familiar.

61
00:04:00,343 --> 00:04:02,363
Is it a spin-off of Sparkling School or something?

62
00:04:02,663 --> 00:04:04,103
Well, color Rika impressed.

63
00:04:04,223 --> 00:04:06,703
This is the otomege version of Sparkling School Life,

64
00:04:06,823 --> 00:04:09,563
where the main characters and target characters' genders are flipped.

65
00:04:09,703 --> 00:04:10,743
Kind of the girl version.

66
00:04:11,083 --> 00:04:12,523
They call it Girl School for short.

67
00:04:12,883 --> 00:04:16,283
Ugh, there are all kinds of crazy games in this world, aren't there?

68
00:04:16,283 --> 00:04:18,523
Why does Rika get the feeling you're not interested?

69
00:04:18,883 --> 00:04:19,943
Oh, because I'm not.

70
00:04:20,363 --> 00:04:23,883
You said it's related to that crap game, and I'm sure it's just as trashy.

71
00:04:23,883 --> 00:04:25,023
That's it, we're in a fight.

72
00:04:26,043 --> 00:04:27,583
Look, I've never played Girl School,

73
00:04:27,723 --> 00:04:31,783
but neither have you when you're practically peeing all over Sparkling School's little sister.

74
00:04:32,083 --> 00:04:34,883
Which means you may as well be peeing all over my little sister.

75
00:04:35,183 --> 00:04:38,403
That's fine, I hope you're happy having peed all over Kobito.

76
00:04:38,583 --> 00:04:40,403
Except Kobito's not your sister.

77
00:04:40,983 --> 00:04:41,683
Not the point.

78
00:04:41,903 --> 00:04:45,363
I don't think it's right for you to decide you don't like it when you haven't played it yet.

79
00:04:45,363 --> 00:04:47,523
So you're on their side?

80
00:04:47,963 --> 00:04:51,283
Fine, I'll decide I hate it after I've played it, and I will hate it.

81
00:04:51,323 --> 00:04:52,983
But then you'll have to accept that it sucks.

82
00:04:53,263 --> 00:04:53,483
Hmm.

83
00:05:01,823 --> 00:05:04,903
Sparkling School Life, Girls' Version 4.

84
00:05:06,663 --> 00:05:09,343
Why are you skipping the opening? That's one of the best parts!

85
00:05:09,403 --> 00:05:10,163
Because it's lame.

86
00:05:10,543 --> 00:05:10,863
What?

87
00:05:11,143 --> 00:05:12,143
I have to pick a name?

88
00:05:12,143 --> 00:05:15,743
Just use your real name. That's what everyone else does. Makes it more real.

89
00:05:15,943 --> 00:05:18,863
But the main character's some tramp who's trying to get with a bunch of guys.

90
00:05:18,963 --> 00:05:21,763
Why would I want to be that? It'd be way better to play with meat's name.

91
00:05:21,783 --> 00:05:23,163
Oh, ha-ha! You're so funny!

92
00:05:23,343 --> 00:05:27,683
It's fun to play the wild girl, but you can also be the nice one and limit yourself to one guy.

93
00:05:27,823 --> 00:05:29,963
It would be fun to see one of them take your V-card.

94
00:05:30,403 --> 00:05:32,623
Well, that doesn't seem that bad, I guess.

95
00:05:32,623 --> 00:05:43,463
Your name is Yohechiburake!

96
00:05:44,283 --> 00:05:46,783
Weirdest name in the world for the weirdest girl in the world!

97
00:05:47,303 --> 00:05:48,003
Ha-ha-ha-ha!

98
00:05:48,003 --> 00:05:51,103
She must still be bitter about the whole Simoponome thing.

99
00:05:51,343 --> 00:05:52,963
I'm so freaking brilliant!

100
00:05:53,523 --> 00:05:54,543
Ha-ha-ha-ha-ha!

101
00:05:54,543 --> 00:05:55,943
Ha-ha-ha-ha-ha-ha-ha!

102
00:05:55,943 --> 00:05:56,963
It's not that funny.

103
00:05:57,183 --> 00:05:57,423
What?

104
00:05:57,423 --> 00:06:01,383
Why are you sabotaging Rika's efforts to spread the gospel of girl school?

105
00:06:01,623 --> 00:06:04,363
All you're doing is turning others away from her tribe.

106
00:06:04,383 --> 00:06:06,343
Oh, I just thought it was a funny name.

107
00:06:06,623 --> 00:06:07,963
Why would you do that?

108
00:06:08,563 --> 00:06:11,903
Because I, uh, look, I said I was sorry.

109
00:06:12,063 --> 00:06:13,863
Rika's not asking you to apologize.

110
00:06:14,623 --> 00:06:17,823
She just wants to know why you would do something wicked like that.

111
00:06:17,943 --> 00:06:19,083
She's asking you nicely.

112
00:06:20,803 --> 00:06:22,023
Girls are scary.

113
00:06:22,023 --> 00:06:29,003
My name is Yozara Makazuki.

114
00:06:29,483 --> 00:06:32,703
Starting today, I'm a high school freshman here at Sparkling Academy.

115
00:06:33,503 --> 00:06:36,183
Ah, the spring breeze feels so nice.

116
00:06:37,783 --> 00:06:38,963
Spring breeze?

117
00:06:40,483 --> 00:06:43,183
Even though I'm just an average everyday student,

118
00:06:43,443 --> 00:06:46,483
nothing would make me happier than having an exciting school life.

119
00:06:47,183 --> 00:06:51,863
My breasts are heaving with hope as I make my way through the gates laden with cherry blossoms.

120
00:06:52,403 --> 00:06:54,463
Did you just see your breasts are heaving with hope?

121
00:06:55,603 --> 00:06:57,983
Hey, that was cheesy, but you don't have breasts.

122
00:06:59,783 --> 00:07:01,923
That wasn't very spring breezy of you.

123
00:07:02,203 --> 00:07:03,243
I'll kill you.

124
00:07:03,323 --> 00:07:05,603
Calm down, heckling is part of gaming.

125
00:07:08,483 --> 00:07:09,003
Ouch.

126
00:07:10,583 --> 00:07:12,743
I'm sorry, I was daydreaming.

127
00:07:13,303 --> 00:07:14,683
Here, can you stand?

128
00:07:15,243 --> 00:07:17,083
Well, that was nice. Who is this boy?

129
00:07:17,183 --> 00:07:20,623
Oji Shinomori, he's a star freshman just like your character.

130
00:07:20,623 --> 00:07:23,283
He's the heir to the Shinomori conglomerate,

131
00:07:23,463 --> 00:07:26,163
which means every girl in school wants to be with him.

132
00:07:26,483 --> 00:07:27,503
Nice to meet you.

133
00:07:27,983 --> 00:07:30,403
I'm hoping this year will be great for both of us.

134
00:07:31,783 --> 00:07:33,563
That boy was really cool.

135
00:07:34,283 --> 00:07:37,063
If I already met someone like him on my first day,

136
00:07:37,323 --> 00:07:40,063
then the rest of the year is looking sweet as roses.

137
00:07:40,063 --> 00:07:45,183
What a sweet, rosy-red year you have ahead of you.

138
00:07:48,503 --> 00:07:51,003
Okay, I'm gonna let you pick which name do you like better,

139
00:07:51,103 --> 00:07:52,203
rosy or spring breezy.

140
00:07:52,963 --> 00:07:55,883
I am not using my name on the flower bed for brains, idiot.

141
00:07:56,003 --> 00:07:57,483
How do I switch it back to the other one?

142
00:07:57,523 --> 00:07:58,903
Whoa, it's just a game.

143
00:07:58,983 --> 00:08:00,963
The dialogue is the same no matter who's playing.

144
00:08:00,963 --> 00:08:03,823
Oh, hey.

145
00:08:04,123 --> 00:08:05,803
So, like, how do you know Shinomori?

146
00:08:06,403 --> 00:08:08,123
Who the hell is this random hag?

147
00:08:08,583 --> 00:08:10,803
Yoko sits next to the player in class.

148
00:08:11,003 --> 00:08:13,103
Refer to her with questions about other students.

149
00:08:13,823 --> 00:08:16,203
Um, I think I'll refer to her with my fist instead.

150
00:08:16,463 --> 00:08:17,523
She's a bit of an a-hole.

151
00:08:17,723 --> 00:08:18,923
She was being nice!

152
00:08:18,963 --> 00:08:19,943
Yeah, way too soon.

153
00:08:20,003 --> 00:08:22,643
You don't walk up to a random stranger and act like your besties.

154
00:08:22,803 --> 00:08:24,543
That is a cocky, punk-ass move.

155
00:08:24,623 --> 00:08:25,543
She's just like Akari.

156
00:08:25,543 --> 00:08:26,243
What's your deal?

157
00:08:26,423 --> 00:08:28,363
Akari's like the sweetest girl in the world.

158
00:08:29,323 --> 00:08:30,463
I like you, Yozara.

159
00:08:30,623 --> 00:08:31,623
Let's be friends, okay?

160
00:08:32,403 --> 00:08:32,843
Sure.

161
00:08:33,083 --> 00:08:34,263
It's nice to meet you.

162
00:08:34,883 --> 00:08:35,903
She is so fake.

163
00:08:36,143 --> 00:08:37,643
She's so gonna stab me in the back.

164
00:08:37,683 --> 00:08:38,463
I just know it.

165
00:08:39,383 --> 00:08:41,643
Low scores in all areas except sleeping?

166
00:08:42,423 --> 00:08:42,863
Loser.

167
00:08:43,303 --> 00:08:44,903
Guess I'll build up her grades first.

168
00:08:47,623 --> 00:08:48,303
That's better.

169
00:08:48,543 --> 00:08:49,323
Almost done.

170
00:08:52,143 --> 00:08:52,623
Hmm.

171
00:08:53,043 --> 00:08:54,883
This question's a hard one.

172
00:08:54,883 --> 00:08:56,163
Oh, shut up.

173
00:08:56,343 --> 00:08:57,663
You're never gonna make it anywhere

174
00:08:57,663 --> 00:08:59,663
if you can't get through level one freshman homework.

175
00:08:59,883 --> 00:09:01,083
Man, I hate this game.

176
00:09:01,143 --> 00:09:01,943
It's not challenging.

177
00:09:03,743 --> 00:09:05,223
You look like you're having trouble.

178
00:09:05,743 --> 00:09:06,983
Want me to explain that to you?

179
00:09:07,443 --> 00:09:08,703
Hi, boy with glasses!

180
00:09:09,523 --> 00:09:09,883
Ah!

181
00:09:10,523 --> 00:09:12,703
Is that like the girl's school version of Yukiko?

182
00:09:13,163 --> 00:09:14,503
That dude kind of sucks.

183
00:09:14,843 --> 00:09:16,683
His name is Tomo Suzutsuki.

184
00:09:16,823 --> 00:09:18,663
He has the highest GPA in the class.

185
00:09:19,103 --> 00:09:20,023
Oh, well, that's cool.

186
00:09:20,263 --> 00:09:21,663
He can help you with homework, right?

187
00:09:21,903 --> 00:09:22,303
Great.

188
00:09:22,303 --> 00:09:27,183
So I think it's great that you study in the library in your free time.

189
00:09:27,403 --> 00:09:29,083
And I can't stop thinking about you.

190
00:09:30,163 --> 00:09:30,583
What?

191
00:09:30,883 --> 00:09:31,983
What does that mean?

192
00:09:32,203 --> 00:09:35,603
He may look like a smart guy, but he's actually just a huge perv.

193
00:09:37,363 --> 00:09:38,423
Get out of the way.

194
00:09:38,503 --> 00:09:39,023
I'm busy.

195
00:09:39,023 --> 00:09:43,883
I admire you for wanting to solve such a difficult problem on your own.

196
00:09:44,183 --> 00:09:47,943
However, there's nothing wrong with asking for help once in a while.

197
00:09:48,363 --> 00:09:49,663
The greatest minds do it.

198
00:09:50,463 --> 00:09:52,903
Please don't hesitate to call if you change your mind.

199
00:09:55,803 --> 00:09:57,603
Does anybody else find him annoying?

200
00:09:58,143 --> 00:10:01,143
Guess I'm gonna have to find somewhere else to study besides the library.

201
00:10:01,143 --> 00:10:02,143
Yes!

202
00:10:16,303 --> 00:10:17,863
Now that's more like me.

203
00:10:18,103 --> 00:10:20,963
Yeah, but it's a dating game and you killed your social skills.

204
00:10:21,003 --> 00:10:24,083
Rika finds it painful to watch someone fail so miserably this way.

205
00:10:24,203 --> 00:10:25,123
She wants to cry.

206
00:10:25,323 --> 00:10:27,143
Even in games, she's a tragic mess.

207
00:10:27,143 --> 00:10:38,583
Really?

208
00:10:38,863 --> 00:10:43,243
You punks must have a death wish if you're coming after me when I have a strength level of 380.

209
00:10:43,403 --> 00:10:44,063
Take this!

210
00:10:44,603 --> 00:10:45,323
What the crap?

211
00:10:45,803 --> 00:10:46,443
Come on!

212
00:10:46,503 --> 00:10:47,963
Why isn't the attack button working?

213
00:10:48,063 --> 00:10:50,743
I think you're confused as to what kind of game this is.

214
00:10:55,223 --> 00:10:56,383
I'm gonna be honest.

215
00:10:56,383 --> 00:10:59,063
Guys like you seriously make me want to puke.

216
00:10:59,403 --> 00:10:59,923
Bastard.

217
00:11:00,603 --> 00:11:01,403
Get him!

218
00:11:08,423 --> 00:11:10,923
You're Yozora Mikazuki, right?

219
00:11:11,523 --> 00:11:12,883
How do you know my name?

220
00:11:13,843 --> 00:11:15,523
You are famous, you know.

221
00:11:18,063 --> 00:11:20,003
The name's Eiji Nagatani.

222
00:11:20,803 --> 00:11:24,103
This ain't the place for elite types like you to be wandering around.

223
00:11:24,783 --> 00:11:25,823
You should go home.

224
00:11:25,823 --> 00:11:32,183
Maybe I should ask him out.

225
00:11:32,703 --> 00:11:33,583
You should!

226
00:11:33,923 --> 00:11:36,423
But does that mean this type of guy is your type?

227
00:11:36,783 --> 00:11:37,783
Of course not.

228
00:11:37,943 --> 00:11:41,003
I'm just trying to make this game more interesting since you're forcing me to play.

229
00:11:41,443 --> 00:11:42,503
So shut up.

230
00:11:42,503 --> 00:11:46,743
Guys like that creep me out with their messy hair, crazy eyes, and boring voices.

231
00:11:46,903 --> 00:11:48,343
They're also extremely rude.

232
00:11:48,503 --> 00:11:49,043
Oh, shut up!

233
00:11:49,043 --> 00:11:50,043
You haven't even heard to talk.

234
00:11:50,043 --> 00:11:50,583
Huh?

235
00:11:50,583 --> 00:11:51,043
Huh?

236
00:11:51,043 --> 00:11:54,803
You mean next Sunday?

237
00:11:54,803 --> 00:11:55,803
Right.

238
00:11:55,803 --> 00:11:56,803
Let's meet...

239
00:11:56,803 --> 00:11:59,223
Um, how about the batting cages?

240
00:11:59,223 --> 00:12:00,683
Sure.

241
00:12:00,683 --> 00:12:02,343
That's fine, I guess.

242
00:12:02,343 --> 00:12:04,703
Okay, it's a date.

243
00:12:04,703 --> 00:12:05,543
Seriously?

244
00:12:05,543 --> 00:12:06,343
Wonderful, Tina.

245
00:12:06,343 --> 00:12:08,183
Let's go.

246
00:12:09,143 --> 00:12:10,463
Wow, you're pretty good.

247
00:12:10,463 --> 00:12:12,463
Anyone can do this much.

248
00:12:14,463 --> 00:12:17,463
You did your hair different today, huh?

249
00:12:17,463 --> 00:12:20,463
Hmm? Did you say something?

250
00:12:20,463 --> 00:12:22,463
Huh? It was nothing.

251
00:12:22,463 --> 00:12:25,463
Wow. He's actually pretty observant for a commoner.

252
00:12:25,463 --> 00:12:26,463
I'm impressed.

253
00:12:26,463 --> 00:12:30,463
Maybe Kotika would benefit from taking some lessons from that guy.

254
00:12:30,463 --> 00:12:31,463
Lessons in what?

255
00:12:31,463 --> 00:12:33,463
Noticing girls' hairstyles.

256
00:12:33,463 --> 00:12:35,463
When they take the time to do something different with their hair,

257
00:12:35,463 --> 00:12:38,463
you should mention it and follow that with a compliment.

258
00:12:38,463 --> 00:12:40,463
I do that anyway. Ask Yozara.

259
00:12:40,463 --> 00:12:42,463
When you cut your hair, I said it looked nice, right?

260
00:12:42,463 --> 00:12:44,463
I don't remember. Why would you bring that up now?

261
00:12:44,463 --> 00:12:48,463
So you complimented Yozara's hair. Rika gets it.

262
00:12:48,463 --> 00:12:49,463
And while we're on the subject,

263
00:12:49,463 --> 00:12:52,463
I noticed you've been changing yours around a lot later.

264
00:12:52,463 --> 00:12:55,463
Did you notice this whole time and never said anything?

265
00:12:55,463 --> 00:12:57,463
You never once reacted, so Rika was afraid

266
00:12:57,463 --> 00:12:59,463
that she was as memorable as a rock on the roadside.

267
00:12:59,463 --> 00:13:02,463
She has lost many nights of sleep and suffers massive depression

268
00:13:02,463 --> 00:13:03,463
because you're stupid!

269
00:13:03,463 --> 00:13:05,463
I'm sorry. Chill out.

270
00:13:05,463 --> 00:13:07,463
It's just there's never a time I'm not watching you.

271
00:13:07,463 --> 00:13:09,463
Commenting would get old.

272
00:13:09,463 --> 00:13:12,463
I can't let you out of my side or you'll blow something up.

273
00:13:12,463 --> 00:13:16,463
It's way too late to win Rika over with that line of crap.

274
00:13:16,463 --> 00:13:19,463
Maybe if you'd worked on your status this whole time.

275
00:13:19,463 --> 00:13:21,463
Status of what? What do you mean?

276
00:13:21,463 --> 00:13:24,463
I mean if you'd spent a little more time building your affection points with Rika,

277
00:13:24,463 --> 00:13:28,463
you'd be going at it with her right now in a loud, passionate cacophony of pleasure.

278
00:13:28,463 --> 00:13:32,463
As it is, your points are very low and she cannot credit you for this mild excuse for a compliment.

279
00:13:32,463 --> 00:13:35,463
If you bring those points up, you'll get yourself up!

280
00:13:35,463 --> 00:13:38,463
But why should I have to win affection points from you? We're friends.

281
00:13:38,463 --> 00:13:40,463
Because I said so!

282
00:13:40,463 --> 00:13:43,463
Uh, wait. Let's talk about this.

283
00:13:43,463 --> 00:13:46,463
Rika is hurt and needs to be alone to practice some self-love.

284
00:13:46,463 --> 00:13:47,463
Okay, thanks, bye.

285
00:13:48,463 --> 00:13:50,463
Uh, what does she mean by self-love?

286
00:13:50,463 --> 00:13:53,463
Exactly what you think. Rika's a pervert.

287
00:13:53,463 --> 00:13:57,463
Another fun day, huh?

288
00:13:58,463 --> 00:14:00,463
Yeah, yeah, sure.

289
00:14:00,463 --> 00:14:02,463
Uh, what is happening here?

290
00:14:02,463 --> 00:14:06,463
I don't want to be presumptuous, but he seems nervous like he might like me.

291
00:14:06,463 --> 00:14:09,463
Well, there are definitely feelings going on over there.

292
00:14:09,463 --> 00:14:11,463
So then yes, he does like me?

293
00:14:15,463 --> 00:14:18,463
Listen, Yozara, I think we should stop seeing each other.

294
00:14:18,463 --> 00:14:19,463
What?

295
00:14:19,463 --> 00:14:22,463
I mean, you're like the school superstar.

296
00:14:22,463 --> 00:14:25,463
Shoot, they even made you student body president.

297
00:14:25,463 --> 00:14:27,463
You keep hanging out with a punk like me.

298
00:14:27,463 --> 00:14:29,463
It'll destroy your reputation.

299
00:14:31,463 --> 00:14:33,463
You are such a wuss.

300
00:14:33,463 --> 00:14:36,463
Who cares what other people decide to think of me?

301
00:14:37,463 --> 00:14:40,463
I'll decide who I want to be with, do you understand?

302
00:14:40,463 --> 00:14:42,463
So you have to stay with me!

303
00:14:43,463 --> 00:14:47,463
I never saw it coming, but I actually feel sorry for Yozara.

304
00:14:47,463 --> 00:14:48,463
Me too.

305
00:14:48,463 --> 00:14:52,463
If she keeps playing, maybe, maybe they'll make up.

306
00:14:56,463 --> 00:15:01,463
I got into a first-rate university, but I didn't manage to get close to anyone.

307
00:15:01,463 --> 00:15:03,463
It was a lonely three years.

308
00:15:04,463 --> 00:15:05,463
It was my own fault.

309
00:15:05,463 --> 00:15:07,463
I should have tried harder to make friends.

310
00:15:08,463 --> 00:15:09,463
That was the worst ending ever!

311
00:15:09,463 --> 00:15:11,463
What's going to happen to Eiji now?

312
00:15:11,463 --> 00:15:14,463
Rika is afraid at some point you must have failed to clear a key checkpoint.

313
00:15:14,463 --> 00:15:18,463
You were never seen interacting with any of the other boys, or even Yoko for that matter.

314
00:15:21,463 --> 00:15:22,463
Oh, yeah.

315
00:15:22,463 --> 00:15:25,463
Don't get too down on yourself about it. That's what's great about gaming.

316
00:15:25,463 --> 00:15:27,463
You can learn from your mistakes and try again.

317
00:15:27,463 --> 00:15:30,463
Next time, you can come on to them hardcore and play the Vixen.

318
00:15:30,463 --> 00:15:34,463
Yeah, no thanks. I'm over it.

319
00:15:35,463 --> 00:15:39,463
If this is what happens when I get to choose how I live my life, that's fine.

320
00:15:39,463 --> 00:15:42,463
But I am sorry that I called it a crappy game.

321
00:15:42,463 --> 00:15:44,463
Girl school was actually fun. I didn't expect that.

322
00:15:44,463 --> 00:15:45,463
Oh, and P.S.

323
00:15:46,463 --> 00:15:49,463
I can barely stand the pansy core guys in my real life.

324
00:15:49,463 --> 00:15:51,463
I don't need to create more in a game.

325
00:15:51,463 --> 00:15:58,463
Hey guys, what's up?

326
00:15:58,463 --> 00:16:03,463
Good morning, Kotika. How are you doing today?

327
00:16:03,463 --> 00:16:06,463
I'm good. You changed your hairstyle, didn't you?

328
00:16:06,463 --> 00:16:08,463
That's all you got?

329
00:16:08,463 --> 00:16:12,463
What do you want from me? I noticed you changed your hair, didn't I?

330
00:16:12,463 --> 00:16:14,463
You did, but what did Rika change about it?

331
00:16:14,463 --> 00:16:18,463
Was it the way she's wearing it, or the color, or did she cut some inches off?

332
00:16:18,463 --> 00:16:20,463
Or maybe it's all three.

333
00:16:21,463 --> 00:16:22,463
Did you trim it a bit?

334
00:16:22,463 --> 00:16:23,463
This is more than a trim!

335
00:16:23,463 --> 00:16:26,463
I know, gosh. I was just kidding. Give me a second.

336
00:16:26,463 --> 00:16:29,463
Oh, you're a tricky one. You had Rika going.

337
00:16:29,463 --> 00:16:31,463
You bought some new hair tops.

338
00:16:31,463 --> 00:16:33,463
It's more than that, jerk!

339
00:16:38,463 --> 00:16:40,463
Okay, Spill It, what's with the bimbo look?

340
00:16:40,463 --> 00:16:42,463
You over being smart?

341
