Absolutely not.

342
00:16:43,463 --> 00:16:45,463
Rika just wanted to experiment with color.

343
00:16:45,463 --> 00:16:46,463
That's bad for your hair, you know.

344
00:16:46,463 --> 00:16:47,463
Not to worry.

345
00:16:47,463 --> 00:16:50,463
Rika used a hair dye formula she created all by herself.

346
00:16:50,463 --> 00:16:51,463
You made it?

347
00:16:51,463 --> 00:16:53,463
Rika is quite proud of this one.

348
00:16:53,463 --> 00:16:56,463
There is almost zero fading or risk of damage in this formula.

349
00:16:56,463 --> 00:17:01,463
And the most amazing feature is you can switch back to your natural color anytime you decide to.

350
00:17:01,463 --> 00:17:03,463
Isn't that awesome?

351
00:17:03,463 --> 00:17:05,463
Yeah, I guess it's kind of awesome.

352
00:17:05,463 --> 00:17:09,463
But if I'm being totally honest, your inventions lately, they're not blowing me away.

353
00:17:09,463 --> 00:17:10,463
Like which ones?

354
00:17:10,463 --> 00:17:16,463
Well, computer software, long-lasting light bulbs, electric pots that boil water without a heat source,

355
00:17:16,463 --> 00:17:20,463
automatic beetle-raising tanks, ice cream without calories, and now reversible hair dye.

356
00:17:20,463 --> 00:17:24,463
I mean, don't get me wrong, they're all very useful products, but where's the sparkle? Where's the romance?

357
00:17:24,463 --> 00:17:27,463
Ryan, what kind of invention do you want from Rika?

358
00:17:27,463 --> 00:17:29,463
Well, I never thought about it.

359
00:17:29,463 --> 00:17:32,463
Oh, I know. How about one of those giant robots you like?

360
00:17:32,463 --> 00:17:36,463
That's a national government-level project! It'd take Rika years to get that approved!

361
00:17:36,463 --> 00:17:38,463
Oh, then how about a fifth-dimensional pocket?

362
00:17:38,463 --> 00:17:41,463
The difficulty level on that one far exceeds your robot idea.

363
00:17:41,463 --> 00:17:45,463
All right, then. Maybe a flashlight that can make things bigger or smaller.

364
00:17:45,463 --> 00:17:48,463
Or maybe like a cloth, and you can wrap it around broken items to fix them.

365
00:17:48,463 --> 00:17:51,463
Or a jelly you can eat and understand any language you want.

366
00:17:51,463 --> 00:17:53,463
Do they make those yet?

367
00:17:53,463 --> 00:17:59,463
No, scratch that. How do you feel about time machines?

368
00:17:59,463 --> 00:18:01,463
What?

369
00:18:06,463 --> 00:18:09,463
Ladies and gentlemen, Rika gives you time machine!

370
00:18:09,463 --> 00:18:12,463
Huh? That's a time machine?

371
00:18:12,463 --> 00:18:15,463
Can you go to both the past and the future with it?

372
00:18:15,463 --> 00:18:19,463
Unfortunately, there's no future mode. Travelers may only visit their past.

373
00:18:19,463 --> 00:18:20,463
You're kidding, right?

374
00:18:20,463 --> 00:18:23,463
If you don't believe Rika, put it on and try it yourself!

375
00:18:23,463 --> 00:18:27,463
Now, don't freak out in there. Rika will bring you back after five minutes.

376
00:18:27,463 --> 00:18:29,463
Um, okay.

377
00:18:29,463 --> 00:18:31,463
Be careful.

378
00:18:31,463 --> 00:18:34,463
Have you ever tested that thing to make sure it's safe?

379
00:18:34,463 --> 00:18:37,463
Rika is a mad scientist! You have nothing to worry about!

380
00:18:37,463 --> 00:18:39,463
Yeah, the word mad isn't very reassuring.

381
00:18:39,463 --> 00:18:41,463
Don't sweat the small stuff, Kotaka.

382
00:18:41,463 --> 00:18:45,463
Now, Rika needs you to concentrate and think of what part of your past you want to revisit.

383
00:18:45,463 --> 00:18:47,463
I know exactly where I want to go.

384
00:18:50,463 --> 00:19:07,463
No way. That's amazing.

385
00:19:07,463 --> 00:19:09,463
What are you mumbling about over there?

386
00:19:09,463 --> 00:19:10,463
Uh...

387
00:19:10,463 --> 00:19:11,463
Uh...

388
00:19:11,463 --> 00:19:12,463
Uh...

389
00:19:12,463 --> 00:19:13,463
Hmm.

390
00:19:13,463 --> 00:19:18,463
Wow. It's really hurt.

391
00:19:18,463 --> 00:19:19,463
What's going on, Taka?

392
00:19:19,463 --> 00:19:22,463
Huh? But I... uh...

393
00:19:22,463 --> 00:19:24,463
Are you having a seizure?

394
00:19:24,463 --> 00:19:26,463
No, I'm fine. It was just some gas.

395
00:19:26,463 --> 00:19:27,463
You're so weird.

396
00:19:27,463 --> 00:19:32,463
All right, well, don't forget tomorrow. I gotta go home now.

397
00:19:32,463 --> 00:19:36,463
I can't believe it worked. I'm in that exact day.

398
00:19:36,463 --> 00:19:39,463
Have a good night, Taka.

399
00:19:39,463 --> 00:19:41,463
Yozura, wait!

400
00:19:41,463 --> 00:19:44,463
How do you know what my real name is?

401
00:19:44,463 --> 00:19:50,463
Listen, my family and I are moving day after tomorrow. I won't be back for around ten years.

402
00:19:50,463 --> 00:19:54,463
So that means tomorrow will be my last chance to see you.

403
00:19:54,463 --> 00:19:55,463
Really?

404
00:19:55,463 --> 00:19:56,463
I'm sorry.

405
00:19:56,463 --> 00:19:57,463
For leaving you alone.

406
00:19:57,463 --> 00:20:01,463
But we'll stay friends, even if we don't see each other anymore.

407
00:20:01,463 --> 00:20:04,463
Except you forgot about her until you came back.

408
00:20:04,463 --> 00:20:06,463
No matter what, I promise I'll never forget you.

409
00:20:06,463 --> 00:20:09,463
And then you couldn't even place her face once you did.

410
00:20:09,463 --> 00:20:11,463
I'm sorry. I really am.

411
00:20:11,463 --> 00:20:14,463
And I always will be. Very sorry.

412
00:20:15,463 --> 00:20:17,463
Not good enough.

413
00:20:17,463 --> 00:20:19,463
I'll never forgive you for that!

414
00:20:19,463 --> 00:20:21,463
Die!

415
00:20:21,463 --> 00:20:22,463
Ah!

416
00:20:22,463 --> 00:20:29,463
I am the demon Astero!

417
00:20:29,463 --> 00:20:30,463
What the?

418
00:20:30,463 --> 00:20:33,463
You'll never expect me now, Koraka!

419
00:20:33,463 --> 00:20:38,463
Please forgive me!

420
00:20:38,463 --> 00:20:42,463
Yozura!

421
00:20:42,463 --> 00:20:50,463
It's all over. Are you okay?

422
00:20:50,463 --> 00:20:55,463
So weird. I forgot. You only left me there for five minutes. It felt like so much longer.

423
00:20:55,463 --> 00:21:00,463
Rika owes you an apology. She lied when she said it was a time machine. It's not.

424
00:21:00,463 --> 00:21:09,463
It's actually a kind of sleep aid that Rika created to give a hypnotic effect to the sleeper so they could dream about whatever they wanted simply by wishing hard enough for it.

425
00:21:09,463 --> 00:21:13,463
So wait, that was just... a dream?

426
00:21:13,463 --> 00:21:19,463
Rika only wanted to pull a little prank on you, but it sounded like she ended up giving you a terrible nightmare instead.

427
00:21:19,463 --> 00:21:21,463
She is very sorry for her actions.

428
00:21:21,463 --> 00:21:25,463
Hey, don't be. I'm sorry for criticizing your inventions. It was never my place.

429
00:21:25,463 --> 00:21:28,463
That time machine's brilliant. You should be proud.

430
00:21:28,463 --> 00:21:33,463
Sure, things got weird at the end, but I really did feel like I was time traveling. It was so awesome.

431
00:21:33,463 --> 00:21:38,463
Most of all, you allowed me to tell her what I didn't before, even if it was all a dream.

432
00:21:38,463 --> 00:21:43,463
Rika is happy. That means you did get to time travel with dreams as your portal.

433
00:21:43,463 --> 00:21:45,463
Yeah. I went back ten years.

434
00:21:45,463 --> 00:21:48,463
Oh. Are you sure it was that far back?

435
00:21:55,463 --> 00:21:57,463
Okay, hold on. I have a question for you.

436
00:21:57,463 --> 00:21:59,463
Hmm? Yeah, shoot.

437
00:21:59,463 --> 00:22:04,463
Why were you talking to Yozara in that dream? I mean, if you went back ten years.

438
00:22:04,463 --> 00:22:19,463
Come with me.

439
00:23:41,877 --> 00:23:44,877
Hey, Taka, isn't this cool we get to do the preview this time?

440
00:23:44,877 --> 00:23:47,877
Things got weird ten years into our future, didn't they?

441
00:23:47,877 --> 00:23:48,877
I wonder what'll happen next.

442
00:23:48,877 --> 00:23:50,877
Well, we say the title of the next episode,

443
00:23:50,877 --> 00:23:52,877
Unbreakable Strange Girl.

444
00:23:52,877 --> 00:23:53,877
That sounds awful.

445
00:23:53,877 --> 00:23:55,877
Couldn't they come up with something more appealing?

446
00:23:55,877 --> 00:23:58,877
I wonder which girl they think is unbreakable and strange.

447
00:23:58,877 --> 00:23:59,877
I'm guessing you.

448
00:23:59,877 --> 00:24:01,877
I've never done a strange thing in my whole life!

449
00:24:01,877 --> 00:24:03,877
I think dressing like a boy and picking on people

450
